Follow `RULES.md` in the repo root. Those are the FEGE site-choking rules (v84, NCCD v6 state) copied from agent `bc-be4dd871-6780-44f4-807d-7266aad9b277` (NCCD FEGE health report), branch `cursor/fege-choke-rules-b277` on `Transport-Network-KPI-Check_NCCD`.

This repo is the Ericsson report. Use the same detection, listing, severity, chart, GeoPlot, UrgentTxBWInc, capacity-only OSS rollup, BusyHour flags, Site List 4H/1H block, Missing FEG Port, Immediate actions, and Comparison rules.

Read uploaded files from the name. `OSS` in the name means OSS KPI. `FEG` or `FEGE` in the name means the FEG port KPI (`RxMaxSpeed` is the choke trace). A physical-site or site-database name means geo, Tech, and Site Type. A thana name means the GeoPlot thana list. Dates, V1/V2, and part numbers say how to combine files. They do not change what the file is. Do not require the old Dhaka or NCCD filenames.

OSS and FEG use the same combine order, kept as separate finals: for each date, merge V1 part1+part2, merge V2 part1+part2, then merge V1+V2. Do the same for every other date. If a later upload uses a different version or part count, follow the tokens in the names. Score the dates inside the files and keep every threshold in `RULES.md`. DHAPT35 and DHAPT48 are the shape pattern, not a name filter.

The counter and column names in `RULES.md` are the Huawei export names. If the Ericsson export names them differently, map them to the same roles. Do not change thresholds or shapes.

Do not build a report until the Ericsson FEG, OSS, physical site database, and top-thana files are in the repo. Skip the Comparison sheet until the user provides the previous FEG file.

Keep the BusyHour column spelling **Chocked**. Do not use Tx Total BW to list or grade a site. Do not read the old site-level OSS RAR; roll cell-level OSS to site-hour and drop L900 (`MID(Cell Name, 8, 3)` starts with `L09`). Report file name: `FEGE_Choked_Flat_Sites_Ericsson_vN.xlsx`.
